# Maps the pretty API paths onto the function endpoints.
#
# The functions also declare `config.path`, which Netlify honours when it builds from Git. This
# file is the fallback for deploys that upload pre-bundled functions, where that config is not
# read - without it the endpoints exist but only under /.netlify/functions/*, and the site's
# fetch calls 404 with no obvious cause.
/api/analyze  /.netlify/functions/analyze  200
/api/narrate  /.netlify/functions/narrate  200
